# weyland-dagster-base — the dagster-webserver + dagster-daemon image (k8s/dagster/webserver.yaml, daemon.yaml).
# PINNED to the SAME Dagster release as the user-code image (services/weyland-dagster/requirements.txt) — the
# scheduler, the UI and the pipeline code must run one Dagster version. Bump them together.
#
# Why pinned (2026-10-01): the Dockerfile used to `pip install dagster dagster-graphql dagster-webserver
# dagster-postgres` unpinned. A routine rebuild (ship of git-c6ece648) pulled Dagster 1.13.25, whose dagster-postgres
# switched SQLAlchemy to the psycopg (v3) dialect without declaring the dependency: webserver + daemon crash-looped on
# `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'psycopg'` and Dagster's scheduler and UI were down ~34 min. psycopg is pinned
# explicitly here for the same reason the user-code image pins it.
#
# requirements.txt is the full frozen set the Dockerfile installs; regenerate it in python:3.11-slim (the base) with
#   pip install -r requirements.in && pip freeze > requirements.txt
dagster==1.13.14
dagster-graphql==1.13.14
dagster-webserver==1.13.14
dagster-postgres==0.29.14
dagster-pipes==1.13.14
dagster-shared==1.13.14
psycopg==3.3.4
psycopg-binary==3.3.4
psycopg2-binary==2.9.12
